Pokémon Emerald 3Ds Dual Screen changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: German layout, berry word order and team EXP message
Applies after 0052-german-ending-tilemap.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

The German variant behaves like the French and Italian ones where the retail ROM
does: metric Pokedex units with a decimal comma, and its own wording for the
port's team EXP message (absent from the German ROM, so it is authored here, as
the French and Italian ones are). German berry names are the fruit alone
(AMRENA, MARON, SINEL) and BEERE/BEEREN is a suffix glued to it, so the count
string keeps the two joined without a space. The move type table needs no
widening: German type names are shorter than the English ones.

--- a/src/item.c
+++ b/src/item.c
@@ -117,6 +117,11 @@
     // Italian berry names already start with BACCA: one word, no space.
     txtPtr = StringCopy(dst, berryString);
     StringCopy(txtPtr, berryName);
+#elif defined(PORT_BRIDGE) && GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_GERMAN
+    // German berry names are the fruit alone and BEERE/BEEREN is a suffix:
+    // one word, no space (AMRENA + BEERE).
+    txtPtr = StringCopy(dst, berryName);
+    StringCopy(txtPtr, berryString);
 #else
     txtPtr = StringCopy(dst, berryName);
     *txtPtr = CHAR_SPACE;
--- a/src/strings.c
+++ b/src/strings.c
@@ -1829,6 +1829,9 @@
 #endif
 #if defined(PORT_BRIDGE) && GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_SPANISH
 const u8 gText_Berries[] = _("BAYAS");
+#elif defined(PORT_BRIDGE) && GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_GERMAN
+// German plural of gText_Berry's BEERE, as the German ROM writes it.
+const u8 gText_Berries[] = _("BEEREN");
 #else
 const u8 gText_Berries[] = _("BERRIES");
 #endif
--- a/src/battle_message.c
+++ b/src/battle_message.c
@@ -63,6 +63,11 @@
 // Italian wording of the port's own message: the retail Italian ROM has no
 // equivalent line (the French one is authored the same way).
 static const u8 sText_PkmnTeamGainedEXP[] = _("Il resto della squadra\nriceve punti ESP.!\p");
+#elif defined(PORT_BRIDGE) && GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_GERMAN
+// German wording of the port's own message, on the same terms as the French
+// and Italian ones: the retail German ROM has no equivalent line. EP is the
+// game's own abbreviation (see the EXP. SHARE item name in the German ROM).
+static const u8 sText_PkmnTeamGainedEXP[] = _("Der Rest des Teams erhält\nEP. Punkte!\p");
 #else
 static const u8 sText_PkmnTeamGainedEXP[] = _("The rest of your team gained\nEXP. Points!\p");
 #endif
